WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.990
Your heart pumps blood through
its chambers with every beat.

2
00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:08.790
Yet none of the blood inside those
chambers feeds the heart wall itself.

3
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:12.010
Heart muscle needs a
constant supply of oxygen.

4
00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:16.200
It gets it from the coronary
arteries, which branch from the aorta.

5
00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:22.470
So how can a fatty streak inside an artery
wall end in a heart attack, years later?

6
00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.910
In this mission, you'll watch
a plaque build up in an artery,

7
00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:27.530
step by step.

8
00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:31.910
Then you'll see what happens to heart
muscle when its supply is cut off.

9
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:37.190
Your mission: explain how a fatty streak
inside an artery wall can end in a heart

10
00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:38.770
attack years later.
